The failure comes from the test runner's synchronous stack-depth limit. A single chain of 250 jobs (50,000 / 200) nests too deeply to run inside one `Test.startTest()`/`Test.stopTest()` pair. The fix keeps the per-execution contract (first 200 Ids, one SOQL, one DML) but splits the remaining Ids across up to 10 successor jobs instead of one. That keeps every job in the tree within a shallow depth (about 3 levels for 50,000 Ids), so every account is rated within a single test. The trade-off is that the work forms a bounded fan-out tree rather than a strict single-successor chain.

