The selector mock never reported `Opportunity.SObjectType`. `Application.Selector.setMock` keys mocks by `getSObjectType()`, so the mock was registered under null. `OpportunitiesSelector.newInstance()` therefore fell through to the real selector, which queried the empty test org and returned no rows. The fix is to stub `getSObjectType()` on the selector mock before registering it.

