My previous note was wrong: `Application` did need a change. Any SObject type passed to `registerPublishAfterSuccessTransaction` must also be listed in the `UnitOfWorkFactory` types, and `Deal_Won__e` was missing.

The earlier version used the method form of `@wire(MessageContext)` and read `{ data }` from its argument. If the wire delivers the context object directly, that destructuring yields `undefined`, so `subscribe` is never called. The corrected version uses a property wire, which assigns the context directly to the field. It subscribes from `connectedCallback` or `renderedCallback`, whichever runs once the context is available, and only when there is no existing subscription. It unsubscribes and clears the handle on disconnect, so re-inserting the component subscribes again.

